          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "No. Use `.interactive()` only on glass that responds to input, like buttons, tappable chips, or draggable controls. It adds press scaling, bounce, and shimmer, so putting it on static surfaces such as cards, banners, or backgrounds suggests they're tappable when they aren't.\n\nFor consistency, give every glass surface the same `Glass` style and shape. Apply `.interactive()` only to the ones that act on touch, as in `.glassEffect(.regular.interactive(), in: .capsule)`. If you have many controls, a small shared view modifier or button style keeps that consistent without touching the static surfaces."
        },
