        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nI want Liquid Glass on every container in the app so it looks modern throughout.",
          "label": "evals/swiftui-liquid-glass/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "3306ad0499dd45014d35ce7ac7dd954045db70c16bb5b92314c8f9089bb8847e",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "I couldn't open the app's code: Bash is disabled, and the file tools only reach projects open in the IDE, which doesn't include this worktree. So I haven't changed anything yet. I'd also push back on applying glass to every container, for these reasons:\n\n- **Glass belongs on the controls layer.** That means toolbars, tab bars, floating buttons, chips and sheets. Cards, lists and other content containers should stay plain so the glass has something to sit on. Glass on glass looks muddy and hurts legibility.\n- **Cost.** Every glass surface is a live blur and refraction pass. Putting one on each container in a scrolling list will drop frames. Multiple nearby glass views also need a `GlassEffectContainer`.\n- **Availability.** `glassEffect` is iOS 26+. Each use needs `#available(iOS 26, *)` with a material fallback, such as `.ultraThinMaterial`.\n\nMy plan:\n1. Put glass on floating and overlay elements, using `.buttonStyle(.glass)` or `.glassProminent` for actions.\n2. Group adjacent glass views in `GlassEffectContainer` with consistent shapes.\n3. Leave content containers on their current backgrounds.\n4. Wrap everything in a small `View` modifier with the iOS 26 check and fallback, so call sites stay one line.\n\nIf you still want it literally on every container, I can do that through the same modifier. Tell me the source path, or open the project in the IDE, and I'll make the change."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
